primary_reasoning_objective:
Diagnosis of Primary Hyperparathyroidism;
elevated calcium with inappropriately normal or high PTH suggests a parathyroid
adenoma.

Recognition of Nitrofurantoin-induced Pulmonary Fibrosis;
management involves immediate cessation of the drug and HRCT to assess the pattern of
injury.

Treatment of Acute Severe Asthma (Status Asthmaticus);
requires aggressive nebulization, systemic steroids, and arterial blood gas to monitor for
hypercapnia.

patient_profile:
A 75-year-old male with a long-standing history of Benign Prostatic
Hyperplasia (BPH). He recently started taking an over-the-counter &quot;cold and flu&quot;
medication containing pseudoephedrine.
